#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/index.rst:15
msgid "Unit Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/index.rst:17
msgid ""
"Unit Testing is a software testing technique that reduces defects in the "
"newly developed features or reduces bugs when changing the existing "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/index.rst:20
msgid ""
"**PlatformIO Unit Testing** allows you to segregate each part of the "
"firmware/program and test that the individual parts are working correctly. "
"Using PlatformIO you can execute the same tests on the local host machine "
"(native), on the multiple local embedded devices/boards (connected to local "
"host machine), or on both. When testing both, PlatformIO builds firmware on "
"the host machine, uploads it into a target device, starts tests and collects "
"the test results into test reports. The final information will be shown on "
"the host side with informative output and statistics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/index.rst:29
msgid ""
"Using :ref:`pioremote` you can start unit tests on the **Remote Device** "
"from anywhere in the world or integrate with :ref:`ci` systems."
msgstr ""
